    /// Open the event stream
    ///
    /// A server-sent event stream. Each message carries:
    ///
    /// - `id`: an `EventId`, strictly increasing per principal. `heartbeat` carries no `id`.
    /// - `event`: the event type, one of the `type` values of `StreamEvent`.
    /// - `data`: one line of JSON, a `StreamEvent` whose `type` equals `event`.
    ///
    /// Payloads carry whole objects, never patches. Events that change items come before the
    /// `today.updated` and `views.updated` that reflect them; until those arrive, Today and the
    /// views may still name an item that has just left, which the client draws leaving.
    ///
    /// The server keeps 24 hours of events. On reconnect the client sends the last id it
    /// applied in `Last-Event-ID` and receives every later event in order. An id the server
    /// does not hold, older than the window or newer than its latest event, answers `410`, and
    /// the client refetches the snapshot. `heartbeat` arrives every 25 seconds and is never
    /// stored or replayed. Clients ignore event types they do not know.
    ///
    ///
    /// - Remark: HTTP `GET /events`.
    /// - Remark: Generated from `#/paths//events/get(streamEvents)`.
